# Activity: OKR Domain Models & SQLite Schema

## 1. Objective & Context
Define domain models and SQLite migrations for **RF03 — Goal & OKR Alignment Engine**. Objectives represent quarterly or annual aspirational goals, broken down into measurable Key Results (KRs) which directly connect to daily habits.

- **Prerequisites:** Feature 01 (Workspace Setup).
- **Target Location:** `crates/core/src/domain/okr/` and `crates/core/migrations/0003_create_okrs.sql`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Key Result Modalities:**
  - `NumericTarget`: Tracking numeric metrics from start to target (e.g., Run 100km total, Save $5,000).
  - `HabitLinked`: Progress automatically driven by completion of associated habits.
- **Relational Integrity:**
  - Cascading deletes from Objectives to Key Results.
  - Many-to-many or one-to-many linkage between Key Results and Habits.

## 3. Data Structures & Schema

### Domain Entities (`crates/core/src/domain/okr/models.rs`)
```rust
use chrono::{DateTime, NaiveDate, Utc};
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use uuid::Uuid;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq)]
pub struct Objective {
    pub id: Uuid,
    pub title: String,
    pub description: Option<String>,
    pub quarter: String,            // e.g. "2026-Q4" or "2026-Annual"
    pub start_date: NaiveDate,
    pub end_date: NaiveDate,
    pub progress_percentage: f32,   // 0.0 to 100.0 (weighted average of KRs)
    pub is_completed: bool,
    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,
    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq)]
pub struct KeyResult {
    pub id: Uuid,
    pub objective_id: Uuid,
    pub linked_habit_id: Option<Uuid>, // Optional link to daily habit
    pub title: String,
    pub initial_value: f64,
    pub target_value: f64,
    pub current_value: f64,
    pub unit: String,                  // e.g. "km", "books", "check-ins"
    pub weight: f32,                   // Relative weight for objective progress (e.g., 1.0)
    pub progress_percentage: f32,
    pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,
    pub updated_at: DateTime<Utc>,
}
```

### Database Migration (`migrations/0003_create_okrs.sql`)
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS objectives (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    quarter TEXT NOT NULL,
    start_date TEXT NOT NULL,
    end_date TEXT NOT NULL,
    progress_percentage REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0,
    is_completed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS key_results (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
    objective_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES objectives(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    linked_habit_id TEXT REFERENCES habits(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    initial_value REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0,
    target_value REAL NOT NULL,
    current_value REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0,
    unit TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '',
    weight REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 1.0,
    progress_percentage REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,
    updated_at TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_key_results_objective_id ON key_results(objective_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_key_results_habit_id ON key_results(linked_habit_id);
```

## 4. Implementation Steps
1. Create migration file `crates/core/migrations/0003_create_okrs.sql`.
2. Implement domain structs in `crates/core/src/domain/okr/models.rs`.
3. Add `sqlx::FromRow` and Serde derives.
4. Export models in `crates/core/src/domain/okr/mod.rs`.

## 5. Security, Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **Habit Deletion Safety:** `ON DELETE SET NULL` on `linked_habit_id` ensures that if a user deletes a daily habit, the historic Key Result retains its numerical value without crashing.
- **Div-by-Zero Protection:** Ensure `target_value != initial_value` in validation before calculating percentages.

## 6. Verification & Automated Tests
- Test schema creation and constraints:
  ```rust
  #[tokio::test]
  async fn test_okr_migration() {
      let pool = create_sqlite_pool("sqlite::memory:").await.unwrap();
      sqlx::migrate!("./migrations").run(&pool).await.unwrap();
  }
  ```

## 7. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] `Objective` and `KeyResult` domain models implemented.
- [ ] SQLite migration with foreign keys and cascading rules created.
- [ ] Unit test verifies database migration passes.
